Using the instructions at: https://mattplayschess.com/build-open-mpi/ as our guide. 
Note that we have a shared file system - that is where we want to build the code
openmpi-5.0.9.tar.gz 

# setup 
mkdir -p /orcd/software/openmpi/{build,code,install} 

# Get the code 
cd /orcd/software /openmpi/ wget https://download.open-mpi.org/release/open-mpi/v5/openmpi-5.0.9.tar.gz 

# untar it 
tar -xzvf openmpi-5.0.9.tar.gz -C /orcd/software/openmpi/code 

# Navigate to the build directory
cd /orcd/software/openmpi/build 

# Start the build and install process
sudo /orcd/software/openmpi/code/openmpi-5.0.9/configure -prefix=/orcd/software/openmpi/install |& tee config.out 
sudo make -j 8 |& tee make.out 
sudo make install |& tee install.out

Finally - you need to make sure that the bin directory is in your path.
The example copies the files to the user's bin directory - the correct approach is 
to add the path to your path.  
NOTE: This will need to be done in every terminal and every time unless the path 
gets added permanently as if done on large shared systems.

echo $PATH
export PATH=$PATH:/path_to_openmpi_bin_directory

